Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 3 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M18;
 the second gap of the cold read of part 1): FIVE SHAPES OF A QUOTATION THAT
 THE LOCK'S READER DID NOT SEE

The lock of the plan reads the page for a quotation of the owner by its shape (part 1 of this series). The
cold read of that part found five shapes it does not see. Main gives them in M18 and has not checked them.
Made again here: each planted line passes the reader as it stood, which is kept in the test, and is reported
now.

  1. the words for the owner on one line and the opening mark at the start of the next. For a line of prose,
     the end of the line before it is read with it. A blank line, a table row or another cell is not read
     across;
  2. the words for the owner AFTER the closing mark ("...", the owner said). The mark's closing is found, and
     what follows is read for a verb of saying with the owner, either way round, or for "in his own words";
  3. guillemets with a space inside;
  4. a dash or a hyphen directly before the opening mark;
  5. plain words in backticks after a word for the owner: three words or more, with nothing in them that a
     path, a command or a name of the code has.

Twins that stay quiet: a question of main's followed by what the owner chose; a seat's sentence that names
him, quoted in its cell; paths and a command in backticks after a word for him; a paragraph that ends
between the words for him and the mark; another cell.

What the reader still does not see is said in the test: his words with no mark at all, or in italics; and
words given to him after the closing mark by a verb that is not in its short list.

On the plan's page as it stands the wider reader reports nothing. The lock passes: 21 tests.
Not checked by main. Tested against planted lines by the session that wrote the mend: eight, with six twins.
